<%- include('partials/header', { title: 'Privacy Policy | LifeLine' }) %>
<section class="wrap policy-page">
  <span class="eyebrow">YOUR INFORMATION</span>
  <h1>Privacy policy</h1>
  <p class="policy-updated">LifeLine handles account and donor information only to support the coordination features described here.</p>
  <article class="policy-card">
    <h2>Information used by LifeLine</h2>
    <p>When you create an account, submit a donor profile, request blood or contact the team, LifeLine stores the information you provide in its configured application database. This can include your name, email, phone number, blood group, age, city, request details and messages.</p>
    <h2>Donor directory visibility</h2>
    <p>Donor profiles appear in directory results only when the donor has a recorded, current consent and is available. This may display the donor's name, blood group, city and phone number so people can contact them. Donors may optionally upload a JPEG, PNG or WebP profile photo; a photo is displayed only with separate recorded consent. Older profiles without verifiable consent are kept in the database but remain private until the donor consents again. Donors can withdraw directory or photo consent and pause their availability through their profile.</p>
    <h2>How information is used</h2>
    <p>Account information supports sign-in and dashboard features. Donor and request details support directory, request tracking and administrator review. Contact messages are used to respond to enquiries.</p>
    <h2>Access and safety</h2>
    <p>Account and administrative pages are access-controlled. No website can guarantee absolute security. Do not submit unnecessary sensitive medical information through LifeLine.</p>
    <h2>Your choices and questions</h2>
    <p>You may update donor availability in your profile or request account deactivation from your dashboard. Deactivation disables sign-in and public donor visibility; it retains account, request and donation records for review and does not permanently delete them. For account or privacy questions, contact the team through the <a href="/contact">contact page</a>. LifeLine is a coordination aid, not a medical provider.</p>
    <p class="policy-note">This project policy is a clear notice for the demonstration application, not legal advice. Review it for your jurisdiction before using the service with real personal information.</p>
  </article>
</section>
<%- include('partials/footer') %>
